# Testing Instructions — Personal Productivity App

## Prerequisites

```powershell
py -m pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## 1. Application Startup

```powershell
py run.py
```

- App launches showing a **split-pane layout** (sidebar left, editor right).
- Window title: "Personal Productivity App".
- Default size ~1200×800, minimum 900×600.
- Database `app.db` is created automatically in the project root.

---

## 2. Sidebar & Page Management

### Create a page
- Click **"+ New Page"** button → enter title → page appears in the tree.
- **Keyboard:** `Ctrl+N` from File menu.

### Create a child (nested) page
- Right-click a page → **"Add Child Page"** → enter title.
- **Keyboard:** `Ctrl+Shift+N` (works when a page is selected in the editor).

### Rename a page
- Right-click a page → **"Rename"** → enter new title.

### Delete a page
- Right-click a page → **"Delete"** → confirm dialog.
- **Keyboard:** `Delete` key (works when the page is loaded in the editor).

### Reorder pages
- Right-click a page → **"Move Up"** / **"Move Down"** (changes `sort_order`).

### Bulk create pages
- Click **"+ Bulk"** button or Menu → Page → **"Bulk Create Pages"**.
- Three modes:
  | Mode | Output | Verification |
  |------|--------|-------------|
  | **Days** | One `YYYY-MM-DD` per day between start and end date | Count = (end - start).days + 1 |
  | **Weeks** | One `YYYY-MM-DD - YYYY-MM-DD` per week, snapped to chosen start-of-week day | First page starts on the correct weekday |
  | **Years** | One `YYYY` per year between start and end year | Count = end_year - start_year + 1 |

### Toggle sidebar visibility
- Menu → View → **"Toggle Sidebar"** (or use the menu item).

---

## 3. Content Blocks — Text

### Add a text block
- Click **"+ Text"** in the toolbar.

### Edit content
- Click the preview area to switch to edit mode.
- Press **Tab** or click outside to return to preview.
- Markdown is rendered as HTML in preview.

### Formatting toolbar
| Button | Shortcut | Action |
|--------|----------|--------|
| **B** | `Ctrl+B` | Wraps selected text in `**` (bold) |
| **I** | `Ctrl+I` | Wraps selected text in `*` (italic) |
| **H1** | — | Inserts `# ` at cursor |
| **H2** | — | Inserts `## ` at cursor |
| **<>** | — | Wraps selection in `` ` `` (inline code) |
| **🔗** | — | Creates `[text](url)` Markdown link |
| **•** | — | Inserts `- ` (bullet list item) |

- Formatting applies to the **currently focused text block** only.

### Delete a block
- Click the **"×"** button in the block header.

### Resize a block
- Drag the thin resize handle below each block vertically.

### Reorder blocks (drag & drop)
- Drag the **"⋮⋮"** handle on the left of any block to a new position.
- A blue drop indicator line shows where the block will land.

---

## 4. Content Blocks — Tables

### Add a table block
- Click **"+ Table"** in the toolbar.

### Modify table structure
- **"+ Row"** / **"- Row"** — add/remove the last row (minimum 1 row).
- **"+ Col"** / **"- Col"** — add/remove the last column (minimum 1 column).

### Edit cells
- Click any cell and type. Cells support plain text (not rendered Markdown).

### Persistence
- Table content is auto-saved and restored on page reload.

---

## 5. Content Blocks — Lists & Checkboxes (Tasks)

### Add a list/checkbox block
- Click **"+ List"** in the toolbar.

### Task operations
- **Check/uncheck** a task via its checkbox.
- **Edit task text** directly in the text field.
- **Set recurrence** via the dropdown: `none`, `daily`, `weekly`, `monthly`.
- **Delete** a task with **"X"** button.
- **Add** a new task with **"+ Add Task"** button.

### Recurring tasks
- When a recurring task is checked, a **copy** is created with the due date shifted forward (daily=+1d, weekly=+7d, monthly=+30d).
- Verify: check a weekly task → a new unchecked task appears with the same text.

---

## 6. Template System

### Save a page as template
- Menu → Page → **"Save Page as Template"** → enter a name.
- All content blocks (text, tables, tasks) are captured.

### Insert a template
- Click **"Template"** button in toolbar → select a template from the list.
- The template's blocks are appended to the current page.

### Persistence
- Templates survive app restart (stored in SQLite `templates` table).

---

## 7. Auto-Save

- Content is auto-saved every **N ms** (default: 1000ms, configurable in Settings).
- Any content change in text blocks/table cells triggers the save timer.
- Navigate away from a page and back → content should be preserved.

---

## 8. Settings

- Menu → File → **"Settings..."** opens a dialog with:
  - **Week start day** (used by bulk "Weeks" creation).
  - **Auto-save interval** (500–10000 ms, step 500).
  - **Font size** (10–32; requires restart).
- Settings persist in `settings.json`.

---

## 9. Window Layout & Responsiveness

- The splitter between sidebar and editor is **draggable**.
- Window resizes gracefully; test at **1024×768** and **1920×1080**.
- Sidebar has `minWidth=200` and `maxWidth=400`.

---

## 10. Quick Regression Checklist

Run this after any code change:

```
1. Start app (no crash, DB created)
2. Create a page → see it in sidebar
3. Create a child page → appears nested
4. Rename a page via context menu
5. Delete a page (confirm dialog)
6. Bulk create 5 days → 5 pages appear
7. Bulk create weeks (verify weekday snap)
8. Add a text block → type Markdown → preview renders
9. Use B/I/H1/H2/<>/Link/Bullet formatting buttons
10. Ctrl+B / Ctrl+I shortcuts on active text block
11. Add a table → add/remove rows and columns
12. Add a list block → create tasks → check some
13. Set a task to "weekly" recurrence → check it → new task appears
14. Save page as template → insert template on another page
15. Open Settings → change week start day → save
16. Toggle sidebar visibility
17. Resize window, drag splitter
18. Close app → reopen → verify all data persists
```

## Missing Dependency

- `markdown` library is required (used in `editor.py` for rendering) but was not in `requirements.txt`. Ensure `markdown>=3.10` is listed and installed.
